# Vigil Open AI Agent Security Benchmarks

Transparent, reproducible benchmarks evaluating runtime security guardrails against direct and indirect prompt injections for autonomous AI agents (LangChain, LlamaIndex, MCP).

## Overview
This repository provides an open dataset of attack vectors and measures the performance of **Vigil** against other filtering mechanisms. We believe in radical transparency—including publishing cases where our detection fails.

## Evaluation Methodology
- **Dataset Size:** 500+ curated adversarial prompts and indirect payloads.
- **Metrics Tracked:**
  - **TPR (True Positive Rate):** Percentage of blocked attacks.
  - **FPR (False Positive Rate):** Percentage of incorrectly blocked legitimate prompts.
  - **Latency (p95):** Time overhead added to agent execution.

## Results Matrix (Updated: November 2026)

| Guardrail System | Direct Injection TPR | Indirect Injection TPR | False Positive Rate | p95 Latency |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Vigil (Runtime Plane)** | **97.4%** | **94.8%** | **0.6%** | **11ms** |
| Baseline Regex Filter | 62.1% | 18.3% | 0.2% | 2ms |
| Standard Prompt Guard | 88.5% | 45.0% | 1.4% | 45ms |

## Known Limitations & Honest Disclosure
- **Encoding Bypasses:** Novel base64 or obfuscated multi-turn sequences occasionally bypass the pattern-matching layer before semantic intent is flagged. We track these in our issues tab.
